Subject: [PATCH] widl: Use the class contract when emitting projected methods

make_contract_value already takes the runtime class's contract. Use its
matching constructor reference as well. Generic interfaces need not have a
contract attribute, and classes using version attributes have none to emit.

--- a/tools/widl/metadata.c
+++ b/tools/widl/metadata.c
@@ -2814,1 +2814,3 @@
-    const attr_t *attr = get_attr( iface->attrs, ATTR_CONTRACT );
+    const attr_t *attr = get_attr( class->attrs, ATTR_CONTRACT );
+
+    if (!attr) return;
